WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.000
To see why the bot did something, open the activity feed. The first line of each item says what happened, in plain words.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Open details to see the rule that fired and its numbers. The rule is the real reason; the sentence above it is a summary.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:38.000
A leg can end by a stop-loss, after a loss. It can end by take-profit, after most of the premium was kept. Or by a time roll, near its expiry.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Skipped means the bot chose not to act, and the reason is written. A skipped entry is not an error.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.000
The trade history shows the result of each close, after fees. Wins and losses look the same, except for the sign.
